In alg:BCD-G-RL for cost function 3,
if the iterates remain bounded, i.e., the condition 5 is satisfied, then 
\begin{equation*}
g(\boldsymbol{X}_{k-1})-g(\boldsymbol{X}_{k})\geq\sigma_{LU}\|g\|\|\boldsymbol{X}_{k}-\boldsymbol{X}_{k-1}\|,
\end{equation*}
whenever the elementary function $h_k=h^{(L)}_{k}$ or $h^{(U)}_k$.

In alg:BCD-G-RL for cost function 3,
there exists $\iota_{D}>0$ such that 
\begin{equation}
g(\boldsymbol{X}_{k-1})-g(\boldsymbol{X}_{k})\geq\iota_{D}\|\boldsymbol{\Lambda}(\boldsymbol{X}_{k-1})\|\|\boldsymbol{\Psi}^{*}_{k}-\boldsymbol{I}_{2}\|,
\end{equation}
whenever the elementary function $h_k=h^{(D)}_{k}$.

In BCD-GLU, BCD-GQU and BCD-GU algorithms for cost function 3,
if the iterates remain bounded, i.e., the condition 5 is satisfied, 
then the iterates $\{\boldsymbol{\omega}_k\}_{k\geq 1}$ converge to a point $\boldsymbol{\omega}_{*}$.

Suppose that, in alg:BCD-G-RL for cost function 3, the iterates $\{\boldsymbol{\omega}_k\}_{k\geq 1}$ satisfy that, for large enough $k$,\\
(i) there exists $\sigma>0$ such that
\begin{equation}
f(\boldsymbol{\omega}_{k-1})-f(\boldsymbol{\omega}_{k})\geq\sigma\|f_{t_k}\|\|\boldsymbol{\omega}_{k}-\boldsymbol{\omega}_{k-1}\|;
\end{equation}
(ii) $f_{t_k}=0$ implies that $\boldsymbol{\omega}_{k}=\boldsymbol{\omega}_{k-1}$.\\
Then, if $\boldsymbol{\omega}_*$ is an accumulation point of the iterates $\{\boldsymbol{\omega}_k\}_{k\geq 1}$, it is the limit point.

Let $\mathcal{M}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^d$ be an analytic submanifold
and 
$\{\boldsymbol{x}_k\}_{k\geq 1}\subseteq\mathcal{M}$.
Suppose that $\varphi$ is real analytic and, for large enough $k$,\\
(i) there exists $\sigma>0$ such that
\begin{equation*}
\varphi(\boldsymbol{x}_{k})-{\varphi}(\boldsymbol{x}_{k+1})\geq \sigma\|\varphi\|\|\boldsymbol{x}_{k+1}-\boldsymbol{x}_{k}\|;
\end{equation*}
(ii) $\varphi=0$ implies that $\boldsymbol{x}_{k+1}=\boldsymbol{x}_{k}$.\\
Then, if $\boldsymbol{x}_*$ is an accumulation point of $\{\boldsymbol{x}_k\}_{k\geq 1}$, it is the limit point.

In alg:BCD-G-RL for cost function 3,
there exists $\iota_{LU}>0$ such that 
\begin{equation}
g(\boldsymbol{X}_{k-1})-g(\boldsymbol{X}_{k})\geq\iota_{LU}\|\boldsymbol{\Lambda}(\boldsymbol{X}_{k-1})\|\|\boldsymbol{\Psi}^{*}_{k}-\boldsymbol{I}_{2}\|,
\end{equation}
whenever the elementary function $h_k=h^{(L)}_{k}$ or $h^{(U)}_k$.

In alg:BCD-G-RL for cost function 3,
if the iterates remain bounded, i.e., the condition 5 is satisfied, then 
\begin{equation}
g(\boldsymbol{X}_{k-1})-g(\boldsymbol{X}_{k})\geq\sigma_{D}\|g\|\|\boldsymbol{X}_{k}-\boldsymbol{X}_{k-1}\|,
\end{equation}
whenever the elementary function $h_k=h^{(D)}_{k}$.

In alg:BCD-G-RL for cost function 3,
if the iterates remain bounded, i.e., the condition 5 is satisfied, then 
\begin{equation}
g(\boldsymbol{X}_{k-1})-g(\boldsymbol{X}_{k})\geq\min(\eta_{D},\eta_{LU})\|g\|^2,
\end{equation}
whenever the elementary function $h_k=h^{(D)}_{k}$, $h^{(L)}_{k}$ or $h^{(U)}_k$.

In alg:BCD-G-RL for cost function 3,
if the iterates remain bounded, i.e., the condition 5 is satisfied, then there exists $\kappa>0$ such that 
\begin{equation*}
\|\boldsymbol{\Psi}^{*}_{k}-\boldsymbol{I}_{2}\|\geq	\kappa\|\boldsymbol{\Lambda}(\boldsymbol{X}_{k-1})\|,
\end{equation*}
whenever the elementary function $h_k=h^{(D)}_{k}$, $h^{(L)}_{k}$ or $h^{(U)}_k$.

If we choose the next iterate $\boldsymbol{Y}_k$ as in 33 such that the conditions 34,  35 and 36 are all satisfied, then we have 
\begin{equation}
p(\boldsymbol{Y}_{k-1})-p(\boldsymbol{Y}_{k})\geq \eta_p\|p\|^2, 
\end{equation}
where $\eta_p>0$ is a fixed positive constant.
